# Copy to edge.env (never commit it), only for funnel wildcard certificates. Set the values of your DNS provider.
# Put each secret value in single quotes, for example KEY='value'. Compose expands $ in a value without them (#302).
# Route 53 on the AWS host: nothing (the instance role). Route 53 elsewhere:
# AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID=
# AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=
# Cloudflare (a token with Zone.DNS edit on the one zone):
# CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN=
# Google Cloud DNS. On a GCE VM, its attached service account is used; elsewhere put a key file in caddy/secrets/:
# GCP_PROJECT=
# GOOGLE_APPLICATION_CREDENTIALS=/etc/caddy/secrets/dns.json
# Your own DNS server, RFC 2136 with TSIG:
# RFC2136_KEY_NAME=
# RFC2136_KEY_ALG=hmac-sha256
# RFC2136_KEY=
# RFC2136_SERVER=203.0.113.53:53
